## Technical Description

This project is a governance, evidence, and controlled-experimentation framework
for multi-agent AI systems. Current repository capabilities include:
- functional governance-orchestration role and capability contracts;
- scoped evidence/verification review contracts;
- scoped security-containment and fail-closed boundary contracts;
- MDAR protocol/loop specifications; the acronym expansion remains unresolved in the current canonical taxonomy unless separately established by an owning specification;
- project-local NIST AI RMF, ISO/IEC 42001, EU AI Act, and OWASP crosswalks whose
  mappings do not establish legal compliance, certification, or conformance;
- Phi-Harmonic Gating and related convergence-pattern research;
- internal evaluation/attestation records whose PASS labels are bounded to their
  documented project-local tests and do not constitute third-party certification;
- NDR Pattern Registry artifacts and provenance controls.

DGAF is an active research and implementation framework. Documentation,
passing repository CI, internal review labels, or standards crosswalks do not
by themselves establish production readiness, enterprise deployment fitness,
security certification, regulatory compliance, independent validation, or
efficacy.

For current scientific/control state, use `docs/CURRENT_STATE.md`. For current
functional authority semantics, use `governance/role_capability_registry.v1.json`.

